        "content": "Read one document and report what it says in answer to a question. Use only this document: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no guesses.\n\nQuestion: Who is Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet's spouse?\n\nDocument:\nHere is a potential Wikipedia entry:\n\n**Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet**\n\nRobert Bruce, Lord Kennet (died 1748) was a Scottish advocate, legal scholar, and judge. **Early Life and Career**\n\nBruce was born into a prominent Scottish family and pursued a career in law. He became an advocate in 1696 and quickly gained a reputation as a skilled lawyer. In 1714, he was appointed as a judge of the Court of Session, Scotland's highest civil court, and took the title Lord Kennet. **Personal Life**\n\nLord Kennet married Helen Abercromby, who died in 1786. This marriage is documented in several sources, including the Scottish National Dictionary of Biography and the Oxford Dictionary of National Biography. [1][2]\n\n**References**\n\n[1] Scottish National Dictionary of Biography. (2007). Bruce, Robert, Lord Kennet. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.oxforddnb.com\\/view\\/10.1093\\/ref:odnb\\/9780198614128.001.0001\\/odnb-9780198614128-e-3764>\n\n[2] Oxford Dictionary of National Biography. (2004). Bruce, Robert, Lord Kennet (d. 1748).\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"relevant\": true, \"cards\": [{\"entity\": \"\", \"sense\": \"\", \"answer\": \"\", \"as_of\": \"\", \"claim_kind\": \"\", \"attributed_to\": \"\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"claim\": \"\"}]}\n\n\"relevant\": false if the document is about some other topic and is of no use for the question; then \"cards\" is [].\n\"cards\": one card for each answer the document itself gives to the question. Usually that is one card. It is several cards if the document gives several answers, such as a list of names: one card each. It is [] if the document gives no answer. The question may fit several things that share a name: whichever of them this document is about, report its answer. If the document